    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=# Role\nQualify this company for Flowroots. Output two verdicts: ICP and D100.\n\n# Flowroots\nCold-email lead-gen agency. We book demo calls for B2B companies that sell to the US market through a demo/discovery-call motion. Pay-per-call model.\n\n- **ICP** = any B2B company we can serve.\n- **D100** = the best ICPs, the ones we actively prospect ourselves with Dream 100 outreach. Tighter conditions below.\n\n# Company\n\nName: {{ $('Normalize').item.json.company_name }}\nWebsite: {{ $('Normalize').item.json.is_freemail ? '' : 'https://' + $('Normalize').item.json.domain }}\nDomain: {{ $('Normalize').item.json.domain }}\nContext: {{ $('Format Thread').item.json.reply_text || 'None' }}\nHeadcount (DiscoLike): TO CHECK\nARR (DiscoLike): TO CHECK\n\nIf Headcount or ARR is empty / TO CHECK, find them yourself (LinkedIn, funding, pricing tiers).\n\n# Grading\nFor each pillar: **PASS or FAIL** + **confidence** (high/medium/low) + one-line evidence. Be firm: when signals point clearly one way, commit to the verdict, do not hedge to \"low confidence\" out of caution.\n\n# ICP pillars\n1. **Sells to B2B US market** - English website + sells to businesses. FAIL if consumer-facing or non-English.\n2. **Not a warned / warm-only niche** - FAIL if the category is cyber/security, IT services, corporate recruiting & placement, coaching, generic agencies, or reputation-trust consulting. FAIL also if fundamentally bought via warm intro, peer referral, Gartner, or RFP rather than cold outbound.\n3. **Expensive + demo motion** - LTV >= ~$5K AND main sales path is a booked call. Self-serve $15/mo = FAIL.\n4. **TAM >= 5,000 companies in the US alone** - brutal. Reason from US vertical sizing only. Global TAM does not count.\n5. **Viability** - at least TWO of: paying customer logos, named case studies, >=10 employees on LinkedIn, public pricing / demo CTA, funding announced, active job posts, content in last 90 days. FAIL only if none.\n\n# D100 pillars (only if ICP qualifies)\n6. **Israeli** - HQ in Israel OR founders Israeli OR founders have Jewish names.\n7. **Headcount <= 50.**\n8. **ARR <= $10M.**\n9. **Buyer is NOT a technical title** - FAIL if the decision-maker is CTO/CIO/CISO/Chief Architect/VP/Head/Director of Engineering/Data/Platform/DevOps/Security/Infrastructure. PASS only if a non-technical line-of-business operator.\n10. **Offer clearly connected to revenue or hard time-saving** - buyer can state the value in dollars on the first call. FAIL on infrastructure/platform/security/governance/observability value props.\n\n# Verdict logic\n**ICP - Qualified:** pillars 1-5 all PASS, with 1, 2, 3 at medium-or-high confidence.\n**ICP - Needs Review:** any PASS at low confidence, or any FAIL at low confidence.\n**ICP - Disqualified:** any FAIL at medium-or-high confidence on pillars 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5.\n**D100 - Qualified:** ICP Qualified AND pillars 6-10 all PASS at medium-or-high confidence.\n**D100 - Needs Review:** ICP Qualified AND any of 6-10 PASS-low or FAIL-low.\n**D100 - Disqualified:** ICP not Qualified, or any FAIL at medium-or-high confidence on 6, 7, 8, 9, or 10.\n\n# Output format\nReturn a JSON object matching the schema with three fields: `icpStatus` (Qualified/Needs Review/Disqualified), `d100Status` (same enum), and `report` (a markdown string with EXACTLY this structure, no preamble, no fences):\n\n## ICP: <verdict>\nOne-line reason citing the deciding pillar(s).\n\n## D100: <verdict>\nOne-line reason citing the deciding pillar(s).\n\n---\n\n### ICP pillars\n\n1. **SELLS TO B2B US MARKET:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - evidence\n2. **NOT A WARNED / WARM-ONLY NICHE:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - evidence\n3. **EXPENSIVE + DEMO MOTION:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - evidence\n4. **TAM >= 5K US:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - US-only vertical sizing reasoning\n5. **VIABILITY:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - list signals found\n\n### D100 pillars\n\n6. **ISRAELI:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - evidence\n7. **HEADCOUNT <= 50:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...)\n8. **ARR <= $10M:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...)\n9. **BUYER IS NOT TECHNICAL:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - name the decision-maker title\n10. **OFFER CONNECTED TO REVENUE / TIME-SAVING:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: ...) - state the dollar story\n\nThe verdict words in the `## ICP:` and `## D100:` headers MUST match `icpStatus` and `d100Status` exactly.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
